      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TIME FOR SNOW (5) made an encouraging local debut here nearly 4 weeks ago when running on late for fourth over 1200m. He maps to settle a lot closer this time from the ace draw, and the extra 200m should be right up his alley. Hard to beat. SUMMIT (2) is a former Waller runner who was brought out of his Queensland stable earlier in the season, and was only beaten by a nose as the favourite at his first run in Tasmania here nearly 3 weeks ago. He will be that touch sharper for this, and can go one better. Follow your money. UNFILTERED (1) broke through for a deserved maiden win here in his penultimate start, then motored home late for third last time out. A clever 4kg claim will have him carrying 3kg less this time, and he should be right in among the hardest to beat here. I'M A MACHINE (6) continues to build his fitness, and will be close to his peak fourth up from a spell. Keep safe in all combos. NORTHERN CHILD (3) strips fitter second up, and will take some pegging back.",
